Mycol Progress
DOI 10.1007/s11557-010-0709-y

Coprinellus radicellus, a new species
with northern distribution
Judit Házi & László G. Nagy & Csaba Vágvölgyi &
Tamás Papp

Key to coprophilous Coprinellus species with pileo- and
caulocystidia

1,2 $ a Pileus with globose, thick-walled or cylindrical veil elements
1,8 $ b Pileus devoid of veil
2,3 $ a Spores nodulose or hexagonal
2,4 $ b Spores smooth
3,0 $ a Spores nodulose, 7-10 µm long $ C. doverii (L. Nagy) Házi, L. Nagy, Papp & Vágvölgyi
3,0 $ b Spores hexagonal, 10-12 µm long $ C. marculentus (Britzelm.) Redhead, Vilgalys and Hopple
4,0 $ a Veil on pileus diverticulate (like C. hiascens) $ C. sp. SZMC-NL-0177
4,5 $ b Veil made up of globose elements
5,0 $ a Spores on average less than 7.5 µm long $ C. parvulus (Keizer & Uljé) Házi, L. Nagy, Papp & Vágvölgyi
5,6 $ b Spores >7.5 µm 
6,0 $ a Globose velar elements on pileus strongly thick-walled and often brownish colored $ C. curtus (Kalchbr.) Vilgalys & al.
6,7 $ b Velar elements thin-walled
7,0 $ a Spores 12-17×7-9 µm $ C. heptemerus (M. Lange & A. H. Sm.) Vilgalys & al.
7,0 $ b Spores 7-11×4-5.5 µm $ C. pusillulus (Svr?ek) Házi, L. Nagy, Papp & Vágvölgyi
8,9 $ a Basidia two-spored
8,11 $ b Basidia four-spored
9,0 $ a Sclerocystidia present on pileus $ C. sassii (M. Lange & A.H. Sm.) Redhead & al.
9,10 $ b Sclerocystidia absent
10,0 $ a Pleurocystidia absent; strictly coprophilous species $ C. bisporus (J.E. Lange) Vilgalys & al.
10,0 $ b Pleurocystidia present or absent, usually growing on vegetable debris, or wood-chips, sometimes on dung $ C. bisporiger (P.D. Orton) Redhead & al.
11,0 $ a Sclerocystidia present; germ-pore eccentric $ C. heterosetulosus (Locq. ex Watling) Vilgalys & al.
11,12 $ b Sclerocystidia absent
12,13 $ a Pleurocystidia present; cheilocystidia globose-ellipsoid
12,16 $ b Pleurocystidia absent; cheilocystidia globose
13,14 $ a Spores 8-11.5 µm long; pileocystidia up to 70 µm  long
13,15 $ b Spores larger (>12 µm ) ; pileocystidia longer
14,0 $ a Caulocystidia unbranched $ C. brevisetulosus (Arnolds) Redhead & al.
14,0 $ b Caulocystidia branched $ C. sp. (SZMC-NL-1752)
15,0 $ a Clamp connections present $ C. ephemerus (Bull.) Redhead & al.
15,0 $ b Clamp connections absent $ C. congregatus (Bull.) P. Karst
16,0 $ a Spores 7-9 µm long and 3-4 µm broad, pileus 2-4 mm high when young, stipe non-radicate $ C. pellucidus (P. Karst.) Redhead & al.
16,0 $ b Spores 8-11 µm long and 4-6.5 µm broad, pileus somewhat larger, 1-5 mm high when young, stipe often radicate $ C. radicellus sp. nov.

